    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "You're right that it can feel like empty words when you're drowning in that kind of pain. But \"stopping the fight\" doesn't have to mean ending your life—it can mean surrendering the *expectation* that you have to fix everything alone. The logic of suffering is cruel, but it's not the whole truth; there are moments of relief you haven't met yet, even if they feel impossible to imagine now. You're not weak for wanting the pain to end—you're human. Please let someone real, like a crisis counselor, hear this exact thought, because they can help you find a way to stop fighting *without* losing yourself.",
